  "security_implications": "prng_key is a masking key for AES. Skipping reseeding (SecSkipPRNGReseeding=1) disables entropy refresh and degrades the mask over time, increasing side-channel leakage risk. The force_masks feature, when allowed (SecAllowForcingMasks=1), can disable strict lockup protection via force_masks_i, potentially making the PRNG state predictable or observable. Both paths require careful external control and parameter discipline.",
  "evidence_refs": [
